## 🔴 CRITICAL BUGS (Exam-Breaking — Data Loss / Wrong Score)

### BUG-001 — Auth Bypass: Any User Can Impersonate Any Other User via `x-demo-user-uid` Header
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Category:** Security
- **Component:** [auth.ts](file:///Users/satyam/Documents/Development%20Log%20/WebMedia/Neet-PG-Crack/src/middleware/auth.ts#L40-L65)
- **Summary:** When no `Authorization: Bearer` header is present, the server accepts ANY `x-demo-user-uid` header value and creates/authenticates as that user — in production.
- **Steps to Reproduce:** Send `curl -H "x-demo-user-uid: victim-user-01" /api/v1/analytics/overview`
- **Expected:** Demo mode should be disabled in production or restricted to whitelisted UIDs.
- **Actual:** Any HTTP client can access, modify, or submit exams for ANY user by crafting the header. No environment check (`NODE_ENV`) gates this fallback.
- **Code Reference:** `auth.ts` L40-65 — `if (demoHeader)` block runs unconditionally in all environments.

### BUG-002 — Race Condition: Double-Click "Start Exam" Can Auto-Submit Your First Session
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Category:** Logic / Data
- **Component:** [repository.ts](file:///Users/satyam/Documents/Development%20Log%20/WebMedia/Neet-PG-Crack/src/db/repository.ts#L866-L868)
- **Summary:** `reconcileUserActiveSessions(userUid, true)` auto-submits ALL in-progress sessions before creating a new one. If the idempotency guard's 15-second window is missed (e.g., slow network, 16s delay), the first session gets force-submitted with 0 answers.
- **Steps to Reproduce:** 1) Click "Start Full Mock" → session created. 2) Network is slow, 16+ seconds pass. 3) Click again → first session auto-submitted with 0/200 attempted.
- **Expected:** Only sessions past their `overallDeadlineAt` should be auto-submitted. Active exams with remaining time should NOT be auto-submitted just because a new start is requested.
- **Actual:** `reconcileUserActiveSessions` with `forceSubmit=true` unconditionally submits all in-progress sessions regardless of remaining time.

### BUG-003 — Timer Drift: `visitCount` Increments on EVERY `persistAction` Call, Not Just Actual Visits
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Category:** Logic / Data
- **Component:** [repository.ts](file:///Users/satyam/Documents/Development%20Log%20/WebMedia/Neet-PG-Crack/src/db/repository.ts#L1589)
- **Summary:** Server increments `visitCount` by 1 on every `recordQuestionMutation` call — including guess toggles, elimination toggles, and second-guess tags. A student who toggles 3 options as eliminated shows `visitCount: 4` even though they visited the question only once.
- **Steps to Reproduce:** Visit Q1 → Toggle guess mode → Eliminate option A → Eliminate option B → Save & Next. visitCount = 4 instead of 1.
- **Expected:** `visitCount` should only increment on actual navigation TO the question (palette jump or next/back), not on in-question interactions.
- **Actual:** `visitCount: existingResp.visitCount + 1` at L1589 runs for ALL action types including `update_guess_or_elimination`.

### BUG-004 — `selectedPendingOption` Can Be an Arbitrary String — No Server-Side Validation
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Category:** Security / Data Integrity
- **Component:** [server.ts](file:///Users/satyam/Documents/Development%20Log%20/WebMedia/Neet-PG-Crack/server.ts#L235)
- **Summary:** The server accepts `selectedPendingOption` as any string from the client. A malicious client can save `"E"`, `"ABCD"`, or `"<script>..."` as the answer option. This corrupts scoring (never matches `correctOption` A/B/C/D) and could cause XSS in review.
- **Steps to Reproduce:** POST to `/api/v1/exams/:id/responses` with `{"selectedPendingOption": "Z", "action": "save_and_next"}`.
- **Expected:** Server should validate that `selectedPendingOption` is `null` or one of `['A', 'B', 'C', 'D']`.
- **Actual:** No validation. The value is saved directly to `saved_option` column.

### BUG-005 — No Admin Role Check on Admin API Endpoints
- **Severity:** 🔴 Critical
- **Category:** Security
- **Component:** [server.ts](file:///Users/satyam/Documents/Development%20Log%20/WebMedia/Neet-PG-Crack/server.ts#L523-L600)
