## 🟠 HIGH SEVERITY BUGS (Wrong Results / Major UX Failure)

### BUG-007 — Offline Queue Replays Can Corrupt Exam State After Submission
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Category:** Data Integrity
- **Component:** [api.ts](file:///Users/satyam/Documents/Development%20Log%20/WebMedia/Neet-PG-Crack/src/lib/api.ts#L94-L122)
- **Summary:** `flushOfflineMutations()` replays queued mutations in order after coming online. If the exam was auto-submitted server-side while offline, queued responses get discarded only if the error message contains `'locked'` or `'completed'` — but the actual server error says `"Cannot modify responses in a completed examination"` which doesn't contain `'locked'` but does contain `'completed'`, so it works. However, **auto-submitted** sessions say `'auto_submitted'` not `'completed'` — the check at L111 may not catch all cases.
- **Steps to Reproduce:** Go offline → answer 10 questions → timer expires server-side → come online → offline queue replays.
- **Expected:** All mutations to already-submitted exams should be cleanly discarded.
- **Actual:** Error message matching is brittle. If server changes the error message, stale mutations get re-queued indefinitely.

### BUG-008 — `effectiveOption` Uses `!== undefined` Instead of `!== null` — Can Accidentally Clear Answers
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Category:** Logic
- **Component:** [examEngine.ts](file:///Users/satyam/Documents/Development%20Log%20/WebMedia/Neet-PG-Crack/src/services/examEngine.ts#L224-L225)
- **Summary:** `const effectiveOption = selectedPendingOption !== undefined ? selectedPendingOption : current.savedOption;` — When `selectedPendingOption` is explicitly `null` (user cleared selection), `null !== undefined` is `true`, so `effectiveOption = null`. This clears the previously saved answer on `save_and_next` even though the user may not have intended to clear.
- **Steps to Reproduce:** Have option A saved → Navigate away and back → Click "Save & Next" without selecting anything.
- **Expected:** Previously saved answer should be preserved.
- **Actual:** `selectedPendingOption` is `null` (no pending change), so `effectiveOption = null`, clearing the saved answer.

### BUG-009 — `secondGuessNotMatchingCorrect` Counts All Non-Matching Second Guesses, Not "Correct" Ones
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Category:** Logic / Analytics
- **Component:** [analyticsEngine.ts](file:///Users/satyam/Documents/Development%20Log%20/WebMedia/Neet-PG-Crack/src/services/analyticsEngine.ts#L253-L254)
- **Summary:** Variable `secondGuessNotMatchingCorrect` increments when `secondGuessOption !== correctOption`. The name suggests "not matching but correct" (contradictory), but it actually counts "second guesses that were wrong." The variable name is misleading and may cause incorrect display in analytics UI.
- **Expected:** Name should be `secondGuessNotMatchingCount` or `secondGuessIncorrect`.
- **Actual:** Misleading counter name may lead to wrong interpretation in future feature development.

