### BUG-014 — Timer `additionalTimeSeconds` Capped at 120s Client-Side but 600s Server-Side
- **Severity:** 🟠 High
- **Category:** Data Integrity
- **Component:** [ExamWorkspace.tsx L297-299](file:///Users/satyam/Documents/Development%20Log%20/WebMedia/Neet-PG-Crack/src/components/ExamWorkspace.tsx#L297-L299) vs [server.ts L242](file:///Users/satyam/Documents/Development%20Log%20/WebMedia/Neet-PG-Crack/server.ts#L242)
- **Summary:** Client caps time-per-question-entry at 120s to prevent idle tab inflation. Server caps at 600s. A malicious client can bypass the 120s cap and report up to 600s per question, inflating their time analytics beyond what's physically possible.
- **Expected:** Server should enforce the same 120s cap or validate against elapsed wall-clock time.
- **Actual:** Server allows up to 600s per mutation: `Math.max(0, Math.min(600, Number(req.body.additionalTimeSeconds || 0)))`.

